This case reports the SHAPE of the allocator's fresh-byte curve for a map
lookup loop, so its output is deliberately different with reclamation off:
"flat" with free on, "grows" with free off. That is the property it exists
to assert, and the *FixturesFreeMatchesNoFree gates therefore invert for it
— they require the two runs to DIFFER.

Same contract as alloc_flat_under_reclaim; docs/ALLOCATION-OBSERVABLE.md
states why the inversion is a claim being checked rather than a check being
skipped.
